# L §4.6 Readings: "A plain read of a reading, x[k] at law date d ..., takes the reading at that instant; with none
# there it is a hole naming the reading and the day (HOLE-NOREADING)" — question "<x>[k] has no reading at
# <instant>" (L §8.1).  "last(x[k], d) takes the last reading on or before d, and since(x[k], d) is the number of
# days from that reading to d": 2026-03-10 − 2026-03-02 = 8 days. "A bound on a reading's age is a rule that tests
# since": L §4.6's quote_now, over px[EUR] with max_age = 5: on 2026-03-10 (8 days) the stale rule wins, its value the
# stated hole; on 2026-03-06 (4 days) base wins, the carry. (Writer 8: `within` and HOLE-STALE are gone, L §2.3.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
unit EUR: currency minor 0.01

input px[u in currencies]: num PLN/u reading
input max_age: int
def quote_now[d in days]: num PLN/EUR at d
  rule base = last(px[EUR], d)
  rule stale beats base = ?"the last quote is older than the bound" when since(px[EUR], d) > max_age

version r
  cite s
  known 2026-03-05
  px[EUR] = 4.3 PLN/EUR at 2026-03-02

version cfg
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  max_age = 5

ask q1: px[EUR] law 2026-03-02
ask q2: px[EUR] law 2026-03-03
ask q3: last(px[EUR], 2026-03-10), since(px[EUR], 2026-03-10)
ask q4: quote_now[2026-03-10], quote_now[2026-03-06]
=== expect
q1: 4.3 PLN/EUR
  law date 2026-03-02, cut 2026-12-31
q2: ?"px[EUR] has no reading at 2026-03-03" (px[EUR])
  law date 2026-03-03, cut 2026-12-31
q3: (4.3 PLN/EUR, 8)
  held: px[EUR] = 4.3 PLN/EUR (r), read for 2026-03-10
  cut 2026-12-31
q4: (?"the last quote is older than the bound" (quote_now[2026-03-10]), 4.3 PLN/EUR)
  held: px[EUR] = 4.3 PLN/EUR (r), read for 2026-03-06
  cut 2026-12-31
